<section class="section-line on-light" id="how">
  <div class="container two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Three parts, no fluff.</h2>
      <p class="lead">We meet one-to-one, by video or in person around Scottsdale. Weekly to start, then as often as the work needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><b>1</b><div><h4>A first conversation</h4><p>Forty-five minutes. Where you are, what you're carrying, whether this is a fit. If it isn't, I'll say so and point you somewhere better.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>2</b><div><h4>Scripture, weekly</h4><p>A passage, a question, an honest hour. Forgiveness, identity, work, marriage, fathering, starting over. We read what God actually said, and we let it read us.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><b>3</b><div><h4>Walk it out</h4><p>Between sessions you do the thing you said you'd do. Make the call. Have the conversation. Put the ledger down. I check. That's the mentoring part.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-line">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow center">What we open</div>
    <h2 class="section-title center">The ground we cover.</h2>
    <div class="onesheet" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <div><h3>Forgiveness</h3><p>Seventy times seven, Matthew 18. The debt you were forgiven, the debts you're still collecting, and how to close the books.</p></div>
      <div><h3>The mind</h3><p>Repent, take every thought captive, be transformed. Romans 12 and 2 Corinthians 10 as a daily practice, not a slogan.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Identity</h3><p>Who you are when the title, the marriage, or the money is gone. Sonship before performance.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Work and money</h3><p>Thirty years in sales and technology. Integrity under quota, generosity under pressure, ambition that doesn't own you.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Fathering</h3><p>Leading children through a divorce, a distance, or your own failures. Repair is possible. I've done it.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Prayer</h3><p>Mark 11. Remember, trust, believe, ask, forgive. Prayer that moves because it's honest.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

